{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Add Persistence","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"text":" plugin and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" macro — no hand-written ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"text":" classes, database actors, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" turns persistence into a declare-and-register concern. You annotate a domain entity with "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the macro generates its SwiftData "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" “shadow” class, the value↔model converters, and the "},{"code":"PersistableEntity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. A generic "},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actor and a "},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" build the container, synthesize one "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per registered "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and reuse the core "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for debounced, batched writes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate plain value-type entities inside an "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"; the plugin observes the changelog and writes through to SwiftData after a debounce. Reads happen once, at launch, into memory — the in-memory "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is the source of truth."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For low-level manual wiring (writing your own "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". For the macro details, see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". To add cross-device iCloud sync on top, see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Before you start","anchor":"Before-you-start","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes a Swidux app already exists — "},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"AppStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are wired and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If not, follow "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a local-only persistence layer. It needs "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no iCloud, CloudKit, or Push entitlements","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — only the sandbox "},{"code":"com.apple.security.network.client","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement if your app also makes network calls (killswitch, analytics, feature flags). Adding sync entitlements to a local-only app is dead configuration and an App Review risk."}]},{"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target in "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPersistence\",","    ]",")"]},{"text":"Step 2: Annotate your domain entity with `@Persisted`","anchor":"Step-2-Annotate-your-domain-entity-with-Persisted","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A persisted entity is a value type that already satisfies "},{"code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"ID == UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" contract). Add "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","    var createdAt: Date","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This generates a "},{"code":"CardModel: @Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" class with "},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"toDomain()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"update(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", plus "},{"code":"extension Card: PersistableEntity { typealias Model = CardModel }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". By default every stored property is mirrored directly onto the model — SwiftData persists scalars "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" composites natively, so no manual blob columns are needed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated model is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"CloudKit-safe by construction","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" model backs both the local and the synced container (see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). SwiftData’s CloudKit mirroring requires every non-optional attribute to be optional or carry a default value, and every relationship to be optional — validated when the "},{"code":"ModelContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is created. "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" satisfies this automatically:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-optional mirrored attributes get a default.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If you wrote one on the domain property ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var count: Int = 0"},{"type":"text","text":"), it is propagated verbatim; otherwise the macro fills a canonical default for the known SwiftData primitives ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String → \"\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bool → false"},{"type":"text","text":", integers\/floats "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"→ 0"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date → .distantPast"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data → Data()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID → UUID()"},{"type":"text","text":"). Defaults are inert locally — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" overwrites them on every load."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-primitive, non-optional properties","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (a custom "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URL"},{"type":"text","text":", an enum) have no default the macro can invent. Give the property a default ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"= …"},{"type":"text","text":"), make it optional, or mark it "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":" — otherwise "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" emits a compile-time error."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Relationships are generated optional","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var tags: [TagModel]? = nil"},{"type":"text","text":"); a non-optional to-one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation"},{"type":"text","text":" is a compile-time error (CloudKit forbids non-optional relationships)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" blob columns","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" default to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data()"},{"type":"text","text":", so any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type is CloudKit-safe through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"entity","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state containers","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" slices). They are different layers and never apply to the same type."}]},{"text":"Marker macros for non-trivial properties","anchor":"Marker-macros-for-non-trivial-properties","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro can’t infer relationships, foreign keys, or which fields are derived. Four property markers (named to avoid SwiftData’s own "},{"code":"@Relationship","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"@Transient","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") tell "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" what to do:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","","    @Inline var styling: TextStyling                 \/\/ one opaque JSON Data column","    @ForeignKey var deckID: UUID                      \/\/ scalar parent reference","    @Relation(deleteRule: .cascade, inverse: \\TagModel.card)","    var tags: [Tag]                                   \/\/ SwiftData relationship","    @Ignored var renderedPreview: String?             \/\/ derived; omitted from the model","}"]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Marker","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effect","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(none)"}],"type":"emphasis"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mirror the property directly (SwiftData persists scalars and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" composites).","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Force a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value into a single JSON "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" column (keeps a CloudKit record compact; sidesteps SwiftData "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-attribute edge cases).","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@ForeignKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Intent marker on a ","type":"text"},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; functionally a mirrored scalar column."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation(deleteRule:inverse:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A SwiftData relationship to another "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity. The property’s type references the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain"}]},{"text":" type (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Tag]"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tag?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); the model substitutes the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"…Model"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow. "},{"code":"inverse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a key path on the generated model, e.g. ","type":"text"},{"code":"\\TagModel.card","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"deleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxDeleteRule"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":".cascade","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".nullify"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".noAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Ignored"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Exclude a derived\/denormalized property. Must be optional so it can be reconstructed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on load.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" does not generate an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Attribute(.unique)"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" — CloudKit forbids unique constraints. Identity is enforced by upsert-by-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityDB"},{"text":", so the same generated model works for both local and synced containers.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"text":"Step 3: Put the `EntityStore` on your state","anchor":"Step-3-Put-the-EntityStore-on-your-state","type":"heading","level":2},{"code":["@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    var cards: EntityStore<Card> = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate "},{"code":"state.cards","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" like any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards[card.id] = card","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.cards.modify(id) { … }"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.cards[id] = nil"},{"type":"text","text":". Every change is recorded for the plugin to drain."}]},{"text":"Step 4: Build the coordinator and register the plugin","anchor":"Step-4-Build-the-coordinator-and-register-the-plugin","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"type":"text","text":", build a local container, create a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator"},{"text":", register its plugin, and run first-load hydration before constructing the store:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured() async -> AppStore {","        let container = try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","","        let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","            entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","            container: container,","            debounce: .milliseconds(250)","        )","","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","        \/\/ Register UndoPlugin first if you use it — snapshots must precede writes.","        plugins.register(persistence.corePlugin)","","        var initial = AppState()","        await persistence.hydrate(into: &initial)   \/\/ first-load: fill EntityStores from disk","","        return Store(initialState: initial, reducer: { … }, plugins: plugins)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"hydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first-load only"}]},{"text":" — it replaces each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" with the on-disk rows before any live edits exist. The only refresh path after launch is ","type":"text"},{"code":"rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which always ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"merges"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (preferring in-memory values) so a “refresh from disk” can never clobber unflushed writes or in-progress UI edits.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 5: Flush on background","anchor":"Step-5-Flush-on-background"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Writes are debounced, so drain them when the app is backgrounded or terminates:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await persistence.corePlugin.flush() }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Multiple-entities-and-ordering","level":2,"text":"Multiple entities and ordering","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".entity(\\.keyPath)"},{"text":" per ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.decks), .entity(\\.cards), .entity(\\.tags)],","    container: try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(","        models: [DeckModel.self, CardModel.self, TagModel.self]","    )",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass every generated ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"…Model"},{"text":" type to the container’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"models:"},{"text":". Writers flush in registration order — if entity B holds a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation"},{"type":"text","text":" to A, register A’s entity first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Testing","text":"Testing","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The whole stack runs against an in-memory SwiftData store, so persistence is unit-testable with no disk and no CloudKit:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let container = try ContainerFactory.makeInMemoryContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","let db = EntityDB(modelContainer: container)","","try await db.upsert(Card(id: id, quote: \"hi\", createdAt: .now), as: CardModel.self)","let all = try await db.fetchAll(CardModel.self)","#expect(all.first?.quote == \"hi\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To prove the rule-#8 merge guarantee, seed the store, make a live in-memory edit, call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coordinator.rehydrate(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and assert the live edit survives."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence"]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"gene